          "solution": "```python\nimport hashlib\nimport hmac\nimport io\nimport pickletools\n\ndef audit_pickle_and_verify_manifest(raw_pickle_bytes: bytes, payload_bytes: bytes, expected_sha256: str, secret_key: bytes, signature_hex: str):\n    risky_names = {\"GLOBAL\", \"STACK_GLOBAL\", \"REDUCE\", \"BUILD\", \"NEWOBJ\", \"NEWOBJ_EX\", \"INST\", \"OBJ\"}\n    risky_count = 0\n    for op, _arg, _pos in pickletools.genops(io.BytesIO(raw_pickle_bytes)):\n        if op.name in risky_names:\n            risky_count += 1\n    is_pickle_safe = risky_count == 0\n    actual_sha = hashlib.sha256(payload_bytes).hexdigest()\n    sha_valid = hmac.compare_digest(actual_sha, expected_sha256)\n    actual_hmac = hmac.new(secret_key, payload_bytes, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    hmac_valid = hmac.compare_digest(actual_hmac, signature_hex)\n    return (is_pickle_safe, risky_count, sha_valid, hmac_valid)\n```"
